<%#
  Global Disconnected Keys setting (#1599): one card on the settings window's
  Appearance tab, after Flag Flash. Turns on the disconnected look, a dim layer
  and a badge on every key that needs the sim, while the sim is absent. It
  replaces the retired `disableWhenDisconnected` checkbox, which promised
  ignored presses that never existed; presses still go through.

  The checkbox carries NO `default` attribute: the setting defaults to off, and
  `default="false"` renders checked (the truthy-attribute trap).
%>
<%- include('accordion', {
  title: 'Disconnected Keys',
  accordionId: 'Global Disconnected Keys',
  open: false,
  content: `
    <sdpi-item label="iRacing not running">
      <sdpi-checkbox setting="showDisconnectedState" label="Dim keys that need iRacing" global></sdpi-checkbox>
    </sdpi-item>
    <div class="ird-supporting-text">
      While iRacing isn't running, keys that need it are dimmed and marked with a badge.
      Pressing one still sends the press. Pit Crew, Switch Profile, Capture CPU Profile
      and the Race Engineer and Radar volume keys keep their normal look, because they
      work without iRacing.
    </div>
  `
}) %>
